   "he": "וּבָאִין וְזוֹקְפִין אוֹתָן בְּצִדֵּי כּוּ׳. תָּנָא: רַבּוֹת, וַאֲרוּכוֹת, וּגְבוֹהוֹת אַחַת עֶשְׂרֵה אַמָּה, כְּדֵי שֶׁיְּהוּ גּוֹחוֹת עַל הַמִּזְבֵּחַ אַמָּה.",
   "en": "§ The mishna continues: «And» after gathering the willow branches, «they» would then «come and stand them upright at the sides» of the altar. «It was taught:» The willow branches were «numerous and long, and eleven cubits high, so that they would lean over the altar» one «cubit.»"
  }
